    OUT_TABLE.write_text("\n".join(T), encoding="utf-8")

    rows = ("| R5-L2 post-event corroboration | Whether speed drop, stillness, orientation change and rotation energy after the full window cut near-miss false alarms at equal recall (V16 H-L2a) or the retraction share (H-L2b). | NOT SUPPORTED: near-miss false-alarm rate rose from " + f(r["r5.l2.held.hL2a.base_rate"], 4) + " to " + f(r["r5.l2.held.hL2a.new_rate"], 4) + "; retraction share fell by " + f(r["r5.l2.held.hL2b.pt"]) + " (3 points needed). | The confirm stage already holds the false-alarm rate at 1%; the post-event features add little beyond the detector score (inferred). | None tested. | An exploratory rise of crash recall at the equal-budget threshold is not a result. |\n"
            "| R5-L5 threshold co-design | Whether re-choosing the early-exit thresholds with the network delay in the objective lowers the 90th percentile of the time to awareness. | NOT SUPPORTED: the best member of the grid is the baseline rule in all three link models; reduction 0. | The confirm stage is fixed and the grid of R3 is small (inferred). | None tested. | A larger design space (the confirm threshold itself) was not tested. |\n")
    rows += ("| R5-L6 crash-weighted placement | Whether crash-weighted gateway placement covers 10 points more held-out (2022) crashes than population-weighted placement for k = 50 to 400. | NOT SUPPORTED: differences " + ", ".join(f(100 * r[f"r5.l6.main.k{k}.diff_crash_minus_pop"], 1) for k in (50, 100, 200, 400)) + " points (positive, intervals above zero, below 10). | The 4 km range puts the gateways in cities where both placements overlap; the population proxy is places of at least 15,000 inhabitants (inferred). | None tested. | Road-length baseline and LoED calibration are NOT_RUN. |\n")
    rows += ("| R5-L8b legitimate vehicles under flood containment | Whether no legitimate vehicle is quarantined in 2,000 simulated vehicle-hours at the measured alert rate. | NOT SUPPORTED: " + str(r["r5.l8.b.quarantined"]) + " quarantined. | Two plausible alerts in one minute count as an over-rate strike (design). | None tested (the design was not changed after the run). | A spacing rule shorter than one minute was not tested. |\n")
    rows += ("| R5-L11a mirror-flip detection | Whether mirror flips of the sensor frame are detected from turns with sensitivity at least 0.95 for five transformations and false detection at most 0.02 (ADDED-AFTER-SESSION-1, own family). | NOT SUPPORTED: both-channel mirrors 100%, false detection 0%, accelerometer-only flips of x and y " + f(100 * r["r5.l11.held.acc_only_x.sensitivity"], 0) + "% and " + f(100 * r["r5.l11.held.acc_only_y.sensitivity"], 0) + "%. | A single-channel flip changes one of two estimates and the estimates are noisy on 16 s clips (inferred). | None tested. | The both-channel result is a limited finding; H-L11b is NOT_RUN. |\n")
    rows += "| R5-L10a leakage in two further benchmarks | Whether UCI HAR or SisFall have more than 1% test windows identical to a window of another split. | NOT SUPPORTED: 0 identical windows in both. | These sets do not share the VZCrash duplication pattern. | None needed. | Other benchmarks were not audited. |\n"
    s = NEG.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    block = f"{NB}\n{rows}{NE}\n"
    if NB in s:
        i, j = s.index(NB), s.index(NE) + len(NE) + 1
        s = s[:i] + block + s[j:]
    else:
        s = s.rstrip("\n") + "\n" + block
    NEG.write_text(s, encoding="utf-8")
    print({h: (round(ps[h], 6), round(adj[h], 6), sup[h]) for h in ps})


